---
// The discovery table from 2026-07-02 — what the domain's records say today.
//
// The factual core of the whole page: it is what makes "email is hosted
// separately, so leaving the mail records alone is workable" a checkable claim
// rather than a hope. S1 re-confirms it before anyone trusts it.
import RecordRow from './RecordRow.astro';
---
<section id="records">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>What's there today</h2>
    <div class="lede">The discovery table, from 2026-07-02. Re-confirm in S1 before trusting it.</div>
    <div class="tablewrap">
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>What</th><th>Value today</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <RecordRow label="Registrar" value="GoDaddy.com, LLC" action="keep" actionLabel="Keep">
            no transfer needed
          </RecordRow>
          <RecordRow
            label="DNS host"
            value="GoDaddy — ns05/ns06.domaincontrol.com"
            action="keep"
            actionLabel="Keep"
          >
            edit records here
          </RecordRow>
          <RecordRow
            label="Apex web (<code>harvardintech.com</code>)"
            value="A → 54.183.102.22 (Strikingly)"
            action="change"
            actionLabel="Change"
          >
            → the four GitHub IPs
          </RecordRow>
          <RecordRow
            label="<code>www</code>"
            value="CNAME → www.harvardintech.com.s.strikinglydns.com"
            action="change"
            actionLabel="Change"
          >
            → nseldeib.github.io
          </RecordRow>
          <RecordRow
            label="Email"
            value="MX → mail.harvardintech.com (HostGator)"
            action="danger"
            actionLabel="Do not touch"
          />
          <RecordRow
            label="SPF / TXT"
            value="v=spf1 a mx include:websitewelcome.com ~all"
            action="danger"
            actionLabel="Do not touch"
          />
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="callout">
      <b>Why this is easier than it might have been:</b> DNS lives at GoDaddy rather than
      locked inside Strikingly, so there's no 5–7 day registrar transfer to sit through —
      we edit records directly. And email is hosted separately from the website, which is
      what makes "leave the mail records alone" a workable rule rather than wishful
      thinking: the two genuinely don't depend on each other.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
